  "published": "2026-08-08T06:11:03.617Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0 - Attribute-based prefix registration.\n\n      * [EntityPrefix(\"usr\")] declares an entity's prefix on the type itself, as an alternative to\n        RegisterEntity<User>(\"usr\").\n      * Collect them at start-up with RegisterEntitiesFromAssemblyContaining<TMarker>(),\n        RegisterEntitiesFromAssembly(assembly) or RegisterEntitiesFromAssemblies(...). You name the\n        assemblies; nothing is auto-discovered.\n      * Both styles write to the same registry and can be mixed. A prefix still cannot be claimed\n        twice, whichever style claimed it first, and a clash still fails at start-up.\n      * Scanning happens once during start-up. Identifier generation is unchanged: no reflection at\n        run time, one allocation, same frozen lookup.\n      * The scanning methods are annotated [RequiresUnreferencedCode]; the fluent API remains fully\n        trimming and AOT safe.\n\n      1.0.0 - Initial release.\n\n      * Identifiers of the form <prefix>_<value>, for example usr_01k2f9v8ta7m3x0qbrn4dzeh5c.\n      * Entity prefixes registered once at DI setup; duplicates and malformed prefixes fail at start-up.\n      * ULID values by default (26 characters), or UUIDv7 (32 characters) via UseUuidV7().\n      * Time-ordered: identifiers sort by creation time as plain strings. ULIDs are strictly\n        monotonic per thread, including within a millisecond and across backwards clock steps.\n      * One allocation per identifier. Roughly 30ns for ULID and 46ns for UUIDv7, against 226ns\n        for Guid.NewGuid().ToString().\n      * Targets net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0. Trimming and AOT compatible.",
